{:db/id 17592186096656 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186096455 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fd901f-e08d-54c5-9cda-68543a3d71a9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a General Exponential Function With a Linear Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf09123-3650-5d6a-869a-8edd8f54206b" :question/math-academy-id "e-460" :question/problem "Calculate  $\\displaystyle{\\int 3^{5+4x}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=5+4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 4\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 4 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {3}^{5+4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {3}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {3}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{5+4x}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fd901f-e08d-54c5-9cda-68543a3d71a9" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186097220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fd901f-e08d-54c5-9cda-68543a3d71a9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a General Exponential Function With a Linear Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9abbe1a2-b532-51a1-80f3-e85520454526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{6x - 1}}{\\ln 2} + C" :db/id 17592186095250} {:answer/id #uuid "b2030311-b93b-5086-ac8a-22c14254a5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{3x - 1}}{6} + C" :db/id 17592186095251} {:answer/id #uuid "f17de8b1-8c36-542e-8869-051ce59fb3e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{6x - 1}}{6} + C" :db/id 17592186095252} {:answer/id #uuid "34308b09-4153-58b1-9482-a404961a3981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{6x - 1}}{6\\ln 2} + C" :db/id 1759218609525